WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.159 --> 00:00:07.160
Once every year millions of people in the
Northern Hemisphere lose one hour of sleep

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:12.040
for one night only, due to daylight savings
time, when the clocks go back.

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:17.700
The health consequences of this loss of only
a mere hour of sleep are astronomical.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:22.590
Researchers, examining millions of hospital
admission records worldwide found that the

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:27.400
rates of heart attack on the day following
the evening when the clocks go back skyrocket.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:33.510
Similarly, in the Autumn, when the clocks
go forward and thus we gain an hour of sleep,

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:38.340
there is a significant drop in hospital admissions.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:44.809
In the 1960s a seminal experiment took place
that had disturbing results.

00:00:44.809 --> 00:00:49.720
Eight healthy young males were hooked up to
brain scanning equipment and placed in their

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:52.920
own room for five consecutive days and nights.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:59.600
The purpose of the experiment was not to deprive
them of sleep but deprive them of dreams.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:05.180
Every night when they slept they were allowed
as much NREM (Non-rapid eye movement) sleep

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:11.349
as they desired but as soon as their brain
activity indicated they had slipped into REM

00:01:11.349 --> 00:01:16.990
sleep (dream sleep) someone would enter the
room, wake them up and get them to do maths

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:21.690
problems for ten minutes to prevent them from
falling immediately back asleep.

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:27.060
The full five nights of dream-deprivation
weren't required to produce some terrifying

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:28.330
symptoms.

00:01:28.330 --> 00:01:34.500
After just three nights of little to no REM
sleep, the participants all showed extreme

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:40.130
irritability and became hostile towards the
experimenters.

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:44.960
They also became extremely paranoid and were
convinced that the whole experiment was a

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:47.850
clandestine government conspiracy.

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:53.530
They began to generally distrust those in
charge and some of the participants accused

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:57.170
the researchers of poisoning their food.

00:01:57.170 --> 00:02:01.890
We all know that sleep deprivation can affect
one’s physical health but do you really

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:05.129
know to what disastrous extent?

00:02:05.129 --> 00:02:10.730
And how little sleep you need to miss to inflict
severe consequences upon your body?

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:15.920
If you don’t get at least eight hours of
sleep every night your immune system’s ability

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:22.700
to function properly disintegrates and you’ll
be significantly more likely to catch a virus.

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:25.660
Your focus levels will also plummet.

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:30.700
Studies show people who sleep less than seven
hours per night are much more likely to gain

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:32.360
excessive weight.

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:37.090
There are two hormones that your body uses
to tell your brain when you should feel hungry

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:38.640
and when you’re full.

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:43.600
Leptin, makes you feel full when it’s released,
whereas its opposite, ghrelin, stimulates

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:45.020
your hunger.

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:50.560
When you miss just an hour of sleep, the following
day your levels of leptin will drop so you

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:56.070
will need to eat more to feel full throughout
the day and your ghrelin levels will shoot

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:58.970
up so you’ll want to snack more throughout
the day.

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:04.720
Sleep less than 5 hours per night and studies
have demonstrated that your chances of developing

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:08.040
type II diabetes shoot up.

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:14.700
Sleep deprivation is also strongly linked
to increased levels of heart disease and stroke.

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:22.110
In 2018 a Chinese man died of a stroke after
staying up for 48 hours straight to watch

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:24.460
the Football world cup.

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:29.400
During the very same tournament, another man
died of a heart attack after staying up for

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:36.150
several days and a third man was found dead
in front of his computer screen that had been

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:39.230
broadcasting a world cup match.

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:44.410
Just for the record, football isn’t indiscriminately
killing people, it’s just that fans often

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:48.990
stay up for days to watch football matches
during the world cup that are broadcast at

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:51.510
unsociable hours all across the globe.

00:03:51.510 --> 00:03:59.380
But there is one side effect of sleep deprivation
that new research has only now fully illuminated

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:02.520
and it is particularly worrying.

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:06.880
Your brain activity, like a car engine, creates
waste.

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:12.160
Numerous toxins accumulate in your brain over
the course of the day but your body has a

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:13.160
solution.

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:19.720
Every night your brain gets a power wash,
cerebrospinal fluid washes over your brain

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:23.720
whilst you sleep, clearing away the toxins.

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:27.290
This process is carried out by your brain’s
glymphatic system.

00:04:27.290 --> 00:04:31.350
To put it simply, if you don’t get eight
hours of sleep per night you are missing out

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:36.770
on some of this power washing, meaning some
of the toxins will remain in your brain the

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:40.690
following morning and over time these accumulate.

00:04:40.690 --> 00:04:46.200
Over many years of sleep deprivation you can
build up quite a nasty stockpile of brain

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:51.850
toxins, the only way to get rid of them is
to make up for all your lost sleep, your sleep

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:54.100
debt.

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:59.940
Scientists have labelled brains that have
a large build-up of toxins as ‘dirty brains’.

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:05.000
Having a dirty brain can cause your brain
activity to become foggy and not function

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:06.270
optimally.

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:13.430
But one of these toxins is thought to be particularly
damaging, Beta-amyloid.

00:05:13.430 --> 00:05:19.410
Beta-amyloid is a toxic protein that studies
show could cause Alzheimer’s disease.

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:24.380
The more you let this toxin build up by not
sleeping the more likely you are to develop

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:26.030
Alzheimer’s.

00:05:26.030 --> 00:05:30.970
In a recent study, scientists injected dye
into the glymphatic system of mice so they

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:37.639
could watch the cerebrospinal fluid doing
its power washing.

00:05:37.639 --> 00:05:44.100
They found that during the day the fluid barely
floes through the brain, but during sleep,

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:49.970
particularly REM sleep, the fluid flushes
through the brain very rapidly.

00:05:49.970 --> 00:05:57.500
Some researchers have even postulated that
sleep deprivation could be the biggest contributor

00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:03.510
to Alzheimer's and that by catching up on
sleep those that would otherwise develop it

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:06.699
could stave it off.

00:06:06.699 --> 00:06:14.520
But the effects of sleep deprivation go deeper
and far freakier than physical health.

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:20.950
In 1959 a radio DJ Peter Tripp thought it
would be a good idea to set a record for staying

00:06:20.950 --> 00:06:25.060
awake and he broadcast the whole experience
on his radio show.

00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:29.900
For the benefit of charity and scientific
research, Tripp pledged to stay awake for

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:39.230
200 hours straight and incredibly he did,
but not without some odd and terrible consequences.

00:06:39.230 --> 00:06:44.090
After the first couple of days, he started
to abuse everyone around him and he made his

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:47.260
barber cry, whom he had known for years.

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:53.430
Then, after 120 hours of wakefulness, the
hallucinations kicked in.

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:58.530
He reported walking into someone else’s
hotel room and showering, then when he opened

00:06:58.530 --> 00:07:04.750
a drawer to retrieve his clothes he witnessed
searing flames raging inside the drawer and

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:06.199
jumping out at him.

00:07:06.199 --> 00:07:12.620
At one point, when one of the scientists walked
up to him, Tripp thought he was an undertaker,

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:18.229
come to take him away and bury him - Tripp
ran away, into the street.

00:07:18.229 --> 00:07:23.090
He started to see faces everywhere and in
the objects around him.

00:07:23.090 --> 00:07:28.550
He began to see spiders in his shoes and got
frustrated that nobody else could see them.

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:35.860
The scientists monitoring Tripp noticed something
very interesting - the hallucinations came

00:07:35.860 --> 00:07:44.150
and went in 90-minute cycles, which matches
the pattern of dreaming whilst we sleep.

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:50.900
It’s as though Tripp was trying to dream
even though he was awake, at the very same

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:56.180
time intervals that Tripp would have dreamt,
had he been asleep.

00:07:56.180 --> 00:08:00.300
With the help of stimulant drugs, Tripp made
it to 200 hours.

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:03.820
Then enjoyed a much-needed 24-hour sleep.

00:08:03.820 --> 00:08:09.199
The scientists hoped the eight days of no
sleep would have no lasting, permanent effect

00:08:09.199 --> 00:08:10.360
on Tripp.

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:14.990
And sure enough, after sleeping he claimed
he felt absolutely fine.

00:08:14.990 --> 00:08:19.919
But it didn’t seem that way for everyone
around him.

00:08:19.919 --> 00:08:25.730
His personality had changed from before the
experiment, he quickly lost his job and his

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:31.840
wife divorced him, who claimed he had become
an entirely different man.

00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:38.360
Sleep deprivation can also kill in huge numbers,
it has happened more times than we probably

00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:39.360
know of.

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:43.860
The Chernobyl explosion is considered the
worst nuclear disaster in history.

00:08:43.860 --> 00:08:47.980
Because of the nature of radiation, it is
almost impossible to quantify the number of

00:08:47.980 --> 00:08:53.550
deaths caused by the accident but it is likely
to be in the thousands and it still causes

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:56.240
illness across Europe to this day.

00:08:56.240 --> 00:09:03.699
It is strongly thought that sleep deprivation
can be blamed for the catastrophe - the engineers

00:09:03.699 --> 00:09:10.220
working at 1 am, at the time of the explosion,
had been on shift for 13 hours straight and

00:09:10.220 --> 00:09:12.610
were severely sleep deprived.

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:21.319
Similarly, in 1989, an Exxon Valdez oil supertanker
ran aground in Alaska spilling 258,000 barrels

00:09:21.319 --> 00:09:28.670
of crude oil into the water and soil, killing
profuse amounts of precious marine species

00:09:28.670 --> 00:09:36.720
including 500,000 sea birds and thousands
of otters, bald eagles and whales.

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:41.220
The third-mate in charge of the vessel, who
made the fatal navigational error had only

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:46.079
slept for six out of the previous 48 hours.

00:09:46.079 --> 00:09:52.519
But if prolonging your own life and that of
others aren’t convincing enough reasons

00:09:52.519 --> 00:09:58.889
to inspire you to catch up on sleep perhaps
one more reason will appeal to the narcissist

00:09:58.889 --> 00:10:01.550
in you and make you change your mind.

00:10:01.550 --> 00:10:04.939
If you don’t get enough sleep, you get ugly.

00:10:04.939 --> 00:10:11.250
Sleep deprivation causes paler skin, wrinkles,
bloodshot eyes and droopy eyelids.

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:15.220
In a study in which participants were asked
to rate the attractiveness of people who had

00:10:15.220 --> 00:10:21.470
slept eight hours per night over two nights,
compared to people who only got four hours

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:23.000
each night.

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:29.339
Those who got just four hours sleep were consistently
rated as uglier and strangely people also

00:10:29.339 --> 00:10:32.350
thought they looked less intelligent.

00:10:32.350 --> 00:10:35.579
So turns out beauty sleep is a real thing.

00:10:35.579 --> 00:10:37.439
Thanks for watching.

